# Cursor / Windsurf Agent Rules — Orion Backend

You are working in the Orion World State Engine backend (fork repository).

## Core Directives
1. Always consult `.ai/RULES.md` before making any code modifications.
2. Contradiction detection must be rule-based Python (SRS REQ-27); NEVER ask an LLM if facts conflict.
3. Facts are permanently immutable; always append a new `FactVersion`, never execute an SQL UPDATE on historic values (SRS REQ-22).
4. Every world query must filter by `user_id` for multi-tenant isolation (SRS REQ-4).
5. All tests must pass before declaring work complete: `PYTHONPATH=backend pytest app/tests/ -v`.

For full architecture and skills, see `.ai/README.md`.
